**Module framing.** The parent built the finite Cayley homomorphism $\mathrm{cayleyFinHom}\,e : G \to^* \mathrm{Perm}(\mathrm{Fin}\,n)$ from a relabelling $e : G \simeq \mathrm{Fin}\,n$ and proved it injective. This file studies its **image** $H = \mathrm{range}(\mathrm{cayleyFinHom}\,e)$ and proves the three facts that characterise a *regular* permutation group:
- **transitive** — some $\sigma \in H$ sends any $i$ to any $j$;
- **free (semiregular)** — any $\sigma \in H$ fixing one point is the identity;
- **sharply transitive** — combining these, a *unique* $\sigma \in H$ with $\sigma i = j$.

Together with $|H| = n$, this identifies $H$ as the regular permutation group of degree $n$ — the concrete content of 'Cayley realises $G$ as a regular subgroup of $S_n$'.
